  "discussion": "The current small, short period north-northeast swell will maintain small surf along north-facing shores into Saturday. A larger, long-period northwest swell is expected to arrive late Saturday and will bring advisory level surf to north and west facing shores exposed to the swell Sunday into Monday. The current small, medium period south swell will gradually decline through the weekend, falling to below seasonal averages during the first part of the week. East-facing shores will get continue to be boosted due to the wrap from the north and southerly swells. As the larger north swell builds in Sunday night and Monday, the wrap from that will have the potential for advisory level surf.",
